# 5. GUI with ImGui

<div class="code-path">Code: <code>examples/c6-cgp-marching-cubes/</code></div>

The objective of this example is to use the ImGui window of the program as the interface of the slide. The
scene is an implicit surface (a sum of blobs and of Perlin noise), meshed by marching cubes at each change of
its parameters. With ImGui, there is no HTML to write, and all the settings are in a single window. In a
slide, two points need some care: the window must be readable on the projector, and it must stay consistent
with the buttons of the slide.

