## ImGui in a slide

- **Readable on the projector:** `?gui_scale=1.4` in the address enlarges the text of ImGui.
  - The value is stored in `project::gui_scale`, which the template of CGP gives to ImGui at each frame.
  - The sections of the window stay closed at start: a long window would go out of the frame.
- **The same variables for ImGui and for the slide:** the variables are declared to the bridge, together with
  what to recompute when the slide changes them.
  - ImGui reads the variables at each frame: it therefore displays the new values at the next frame, without
    any additional code.
- **The mouse:** in CGP, ImGui takes the clicks over its window; everywhere else, the mouse rotates the camera.

Two controls of the original window are hidden on the web:

- the wireframe, which uses `glPolygonMode` (see the note of [example 4](../05_buttons/index.html));
- the export of the mesh to a file, which would be written in the memory of the page.

